 \textbf{Release fences.} Android's BufferQueue lets a consumer release a pooled buffer with a fence while still reading it~\cite{bufferqueue}, and NvSciStream returns a multicast packet to its pool once every consumer has released it~\cite{nvscistream}. BIM's borrow bits follow the same per-consumer protocol, and ReadSeal adds where the fence goes, deriving from each recipient's model where its reads end.
 
-\textbf{Asynchronous buffer protocols.} Simpson's four-slot mechanism separates concurrent reads and writes across buffers, and Kopetz and Reisinger's NBW protocol detects overlapping writes and also provides a multibuffer variant~\cite{simpson,nbw,rushbyfour}. Cyclical asynchronous buffers let readers acquire the latest complete value without blocking the writer~\cite{buttazzocab}. BIM instead preserves the particular frame already assigned to each recipient, including while its GPU reads are unsubmitted.
